<http://w3id.org/rml/shapes/RMLTriplesMapShape> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#message> "\n    Triples Map requires exactly one rml:subject or one rml:subjectMap and zero\n    or more rml:predicateObjectMaps.\n    " .
_:n9cf61a9027f64febb5a4ae3bbc98fda8b1 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#minCount> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
_:na88f72710874431c9cbfdbb5f2369607b9 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path> <http://w3id.org/rml/constant> .
_:n3d3f8d29fd184eaf9d3dcdb4a797ec0cb6 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#description> "\n        Inclusion (and ForeignKey) annotations targeting this logical view\n        via rml:targetView. Reached via the inverse of rml:targetView, not\n        rml:structuralAnnotation -- an InclusionAnnotation is the SUBJECT\n        of rml:targetView, not this view's own value, so it isn't\n        otherwise reachable from here; without this property it would\n        never get checked at all.\n        " .
_:nd34f376badc7400287b4bafcb64e693cb9 <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#datatype> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
